## The Shape That Earns Its Place Every Time

Almond isn't a trend. It's a standard the nail shape that keeps reappearing because it solves most of the problems people bring to a salon appointment. It lengthens, it flatters, it frames design without competing with it. The 2026 version simply wears shorter and pairs with finishes that let the shape do the talking.

If you've been considering it: the short almond removes every length barrier that was holding you back. If you've worn it for years: the modern chrome or aura pairing is worth trying. The shape itself hasn't changed just the context it's worn in.

